From: Johannes Stein <johannesstein@freeze-dev.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:01:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 18/75] x86 OptPass2Movx: do not narrow SAR unless the value
 fits the smaller signed range

The register-size optimisation assumed SAR after MOVZX behaves like SHR,
which holds at the original size only. Narrowed, SAR copies the sign bit of
the smaller register: notb %bl; movzbl %bl,%ebx; sarl $1,%ebx became
notb %bl; sarb $1,%bl, so Byte(SarLongint(LongInt(Byte(not B)), 1)) gave
252 instead of 124 for B=6 at -O2 (3.2.x is not affected).
---
 compiler/x86/aoptx86.pas | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/compiler/x86/aoptx86.pas b/compiler/x86/aoptx86.pas
index 3e004cf9..99bde2e7 100644
--- a/compiler/x86/aoptx86.pas
+++ b/compiler/x86/aoptx86.pas
@@ -12784,6 +12784,14 @@ unit aoptx86;
                     { The first instruction was MOVZX, so the value won't be negative }
                     A_SAR:
                       begin
+                        { Done in a smaller register, SAR copies the sign bit of that
+                          size: only equivalent while the value fits its signed range
+                          (e.g. notb/movzbl/sarl $1 must not become notb/sarb $1) }
+                        if (taicpu(hp1).opcode = A_SAR) and
+                          ((TestValMin < 0) or (TestValMax > SignedLowerLimit) or
+                           (TestValSignedMax > SignedLowerLimit)) then
+                          Break;
+
                         if InstrMax <> -1 then
                           BitwiseOnly := False
                         else
